data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Developing the Methodology**\n\nI'm now iterating to develop a 3-step approach that balances brevity and accuracy. The previous idea was too complex, focusing on households and tuning frequency. I am revising my approach to center on the supply side, but still need to find a way to *estimate*, not just *count*.\n\nI've discarded my earlier demand-side idea because it requires too much external data to be useful. I'm focusing on the supply-side question of \"How many advertise?\". My goal is to find a way to extrapolate from my initial search to get a reasonable proxy for the true population.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 21,"totalTokenCount": 447,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 21}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 426,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-2.5-flash","responseId": "AG8raqakJ8X04-EP9P70gA4"}

